: Troubleshooting Prometheus
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Use promtool to validate and check Prometheus configuration files
Identify and troubleshoot common Prometheus scraping issues
Diagnose configuration problems using Prometheus debugging tools
Implement fixes for typical Prometheus deployment issues
Understand Prometheus logging and error reporting mechanisms
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with YAML configuration file format
Basic knowledge of Prometheus concepts (metrics, targets, scraping)
Understanding of HTTP status codes and networking basics
Experience with text editors like nano or vim
